{
"segments": [
{
"text": "Case Two.",
"start": 0.75,
"end": 1.71,
"pause": 0.6
},
{
"text": "The Lemonade on the Lawn.",
"start": 2.31,
"end": 3.867,
"pause": 1.4
},
{
"text": "It was the hottest afternoon of the summer, the kind of day when even the gulls sat still.",
"start": 5.267,
"end": 10.195,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "Loveday Nance was holding a garden party at her cottage on the hill, and half the village was there. Loveday had made a great glass jug of lemonade, and at a quarter past one she went round the lawn filling glasses and dropping in ice cubes from a big bowl. By two o'clock the bowl was empty, and the ice in everybody's glasses had melted away to nothing. The only ice left anywhere was in the freezer in Loveday's kitchen.",
"start": 11.045,
"end": 36.197,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "On the kitchen windowsill sat a silver locket that had belonged to Loveday's grandmother. Loveday had taken it out to show a friend, and she saw it on the sill at two o'clock. At half past two, it was gone.",
"start": 37.047,
"end": 49.933,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "Agnes Bell had just arrived with Captain Quill, the harbourmaster. She had spent the whole afternoon since one o'clock in his harbour office, helping him with his accounts, and then they had walked up the lane together. They had not been out of each other's sight all afternoon.",
"start": 50.783,
"end": 66.74,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "Agnes found Loveday in a fluster and went with her around the garden.",
"start": 67.59,
"end": 71.494,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "Demelza Rowe was in a deckchair by the roses with her sunhat over her face. Three different guests said she had been asleep there since before two, snoring gently, and that nobody had been able to wake her for cake.",
"start": 72.344,
"end": 85.187,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "Then there was Mr Bramble, a holidaymaker who was renting the cottage next door. He sat on a bench in the shade with a full glass of lemonade in his hand. The glass was frosty, and the ice cubes in it were large and sharp at the edges.",
"start": 86.037,
"end": 100.863,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "\"Locket? I've no idea,\" he said. \"I've been sitting right here on this bench for the past hour with my lemonade. Haven't moved an inch. Far too hot.\"",
"start": 101.713,
"end": 111.036,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "Agnes looked at his glass, then up at the blazing sun.",
"start": 111.886,
"end": 115.086,
"pause": 1.1
},
{
"text": "Can you solve it? Who took the silver locket?",
"start": 116.186,
"end": 118.789,
"pause": 1.2
},
{
"text": "Think about it.",
"start": 119.989,
"end": 121.013,
"pause": 0.9
},
{
"text": "Take a moment, or pause here if you are listening. When you are ready, the solution follows.",
"start": 121.913,
"end": 127.139,
"pause": 4.5
},
{
"text": "The Solution.",
"start": 131.639,
"end": 132.663,
"pause": 1.1
},
{
"text": "Mr Bramble took the locket.",
"start": 133.763,
"end": 135.662,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "He said he had been sitting in the sun with the same glass of lemonade for an hour. But on the hottest afternoon of the summer, every other guest's ice had melted away completely. His ice cubes were still large and sharp edged, and his glass was frosty. That ice had been in the glass for a few minutes at most.",
"start": 136.512,
"end": 155.328,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "And the bowl outside had been empty since two o'clock. The only ice left was in the freezer in Loveday's kitchen, right beside the windowsill where the locket had been. Mr Bramble had been in the kitchen very recently.",
"start": 156.178,
"end": 169.81,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "Demelza had been asleep in full view of the guests, and Captain Quill had been with Agnes at the harbour the whole afternoon.",
"start": 170.66,
"end": 177.807,
"pause": 0.85
},
{
"text": "Mr Bramble went red and handed the locket over from his jacket pocket. He collected old lockets, he said, and he had only meant to look at it in the light. Loveday said that next time he could simply ask, and she poured him a fresh glass anyway.",
"start": 178.657,
"end": 193.569,
"pause": 0.0
}
],
